{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Blessed of sons be Asher.</b> That all the sons bless him, as he says, יהי רצוי אחיו — and why? Because he dips his foot in oil, that his land flow with oil and he supplies oil to all his brothers, and this is גוש חלב — that it be in his portion, as explained in ויחי יעקב. And the Rabbi, Rabbi Eliyahu HaKohen, explains in the name of his uncle, the Rabbi, Rabbi Moshe: therefore it says 'blessed of sons,' for examine and you will find that he is abundant in population in the census of Phinehas — according to the census of the wilderness, more than the sons of his other brothers, and this is that he was blessed with sons more than his other brothers."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:04.043094222Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}